- x} = 1 + x + x^{2} + x^{3} + ⋯, x ∈ (-1, 1)$\nusing sigma notation." 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186064483 1071 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1-x}=1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯\\,,\\,x\\in (-1,1)\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186064483 1074 "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =1 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =x \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{0} \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={x}^{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186064486 1068 #edb/ref 17592186061116 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186064486 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253194 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186064486 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186064486 1071 "$\\int \\frac{3}{(1-3x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186064486 1071 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(3)/((1 - 3x)^{3})dx$?" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186064486 1074 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 3(1-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3(1-3x)^{-3} & =3\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-2)}{u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-3x)^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(1-3x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(1-3x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)(1-3x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-(1-3x)^{-3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3(1-3x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(1-3x)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186068850 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253531 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186073820 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253533 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078444 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253269 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078446 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253270 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078446 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253271 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253273 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253329 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253330 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253331 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253332 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078473 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253289 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078473 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253292 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078522 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253293 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078522 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253294 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186078530 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253286 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [1759218607