[17592186166866 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253644 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186166866 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253645 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186166867 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253663 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186166867 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253664 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186166867 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253665 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253450 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172024 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253444 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172024 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253671 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172024 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253673 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253523 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253524 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172041 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253571 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172042 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253574 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172043 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253568 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172043 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253570 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172044 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253595 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172045 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253601 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172045 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253603 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172045 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253607 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172046 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253579 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172047 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253610 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172047 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253611 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172047 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253613 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253670 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186168513 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186172280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253229 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172280 1071 "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3x^{2} + 6x + 4y + 15 = 0$." 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186172280 1071 "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15=0.$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186172280 1074 "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+6x & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2x] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[(x+1)^{2}-1] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2}-3 & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-15+3 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-12 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})(y+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-1,-3).$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186175927 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253438 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186175927 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253439 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186175927 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253440 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186175963 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253618 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186175963 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253619 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253441 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253442 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253443 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253490 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253491 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253492 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253493 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253616 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176026 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253617 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176027 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253494 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176027 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253495 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176027 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253496 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186176027 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253615 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179683 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253620 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179683 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253621 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179811 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253497 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179811 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253498 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179811 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253599 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179812 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253499 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179812 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253631 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179812 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253632 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179813 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253504 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179813 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253505 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179813 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253506 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186179813 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253593 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184148 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253586 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253419 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253420 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253431 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253432 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253433 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253418 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184459 1068 #edb/ref 17592186180901 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186184459 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253240 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184459 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184459 1071 "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v$, we have\n$\\sin u =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}, \\cos u = \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}, \\cos v =-\\frac{5}{6}$.\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, and\n$\\sin (u - v) = \\frac{a\\sqrt{5} - b}{24}$,\n\ncalculate the value of $a + b$." 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186184459 1071 "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{5}-b}{24},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186184459 1074 "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{36}-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{36}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4})(-\\frac{5}{6})-(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{24}-\\frac{11}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-11}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=5,b=11,$ and $a+b=16.$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186192842 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253557 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186198252 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253483 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203967 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253377 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203967 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253378 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203967 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253379 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203968 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253381 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203968 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253382 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203969 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253380 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186203969 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253383 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233258 1068 #edb/ref 17592186252999 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233260 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253076 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233260 1071 "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\n- $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$\n- $8{y}^{′}-xy=3$\n- $3{y}^{″}=4y,\\,y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233260 1071 "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nI. - $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{'}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$\nII. - $8{y}^{'}-xy=3$\nIII. - $3{y}^{''}=4y,\\,y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{'}(-1)=1$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233260 1074 "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{'}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{''}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{'}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233260 1074 "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{″}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233283 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253000 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233283 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{{sin}^{2}x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}-1$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233283 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-1$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233283 1074 "First, we rewrite the numerator of the first term using $1-{cos}^{2}x={sin}^{2}x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}-1=\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}-1\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator of the first term as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}-1 & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}x)}{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}x)}(1+\\operatorname{cos}x)}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}x}}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}x}{1}-1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}x-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233283 1074 "First, we rewrite the numerator of the first term using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-1=\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-1\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator of the first term as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-1 & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1}-1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233288 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253004 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233288 1071 "$10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘})=$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233288 1071 "$10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘})=$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 true] [17592186233288 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533396 17592186045585 false] [17592186233288 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & 